content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-109 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-23500",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 85°C by handheld IR. The applicable manual limits are for bearing-housing surface temperature: normal up to 70°C, alarm at 80°C and trip at 90°C. The reading is therefore 15°C above normal, 5°C above the alarm limit and 5°C below trip. Because it is above the manufacturer's alarm limit, site rules require a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The applicable vibration classification is Figure 3: vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. If the reported 2.5 mm/s is that measurand, it falls in Zone A (0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS, 'New machines'), 0.3 mm/s below the Zone A/B boundary. It is not in restricted Zone C or the highest-severity Zone D.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The overall vibration classification is provisional: the manual requires weekly measurements on both bearing housings and classification of the highest reading, while the report supplies only one reading without identifying its housing or confirming RMS measurement. The supplied evidence therefore does not document a Zone D immediate-stop condition; together with 85°C being below the 90°C trip value, this supports not ordering an immediate stop on the current readings alone. The temperature alarm still requires P1 action.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing — listed first in the manual's troubleshooting entry for high bearing temperature; check grease quantity. The evidence does not establish a quantitative probability ranking.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear — a documented cause of high bearing temperature; inspect the bearings and replace them if worn. Normal reported vibration and absence of noise do not by themselves establish or exclude wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment — a documented cause of high bearing temperature; check alignment and correct it to the manual tolerances.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Raise and execute this as a P1 work order within the shift because the bearing temperature is above the 80°C alarm limit. Before repair, confirm the housing-surface temperature and measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings; confirm that values are mm/s RMS, record locations, and classify the highest vibration reading using Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Troubleshoot the high temperature by checking grease quantity, assessing bearing condition and checking shaft alignment. Do not infer the cause solely from the low reported vibration or absence of noise.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before internal pump work, isolate and drain the pump. Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, drain and vent, and obtain the line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly is removed, use its back pull-out arrangement without disturbing the casing or pipework. Treat the 68 kg assembly as a lift over the 25 kg site threshold: obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings. If bearing replacement is required, apply section 5.3 and replace both bearings as a pair when either shows wear, noise or high temperature; do not replace only the drive-end bearing. Use HF3-512 at the drive end and HF3-510 at the non-drive end.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Where bearing-housing bolts are disturbed, tighten the M12 fasteners to 85 Nm with lightly oiled threads, as specified in Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the scope expands to mechanical-seal work, apply SB-2026-014 for this serial: do not fit HF3-450; fit pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, with no sleeve measurement needed, and tighten its seal gland nuts to 30 Nm rather than the manual's 25 Nm. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. If the casing is opened, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "At closeout, record bearing-housing surface temperature and vibration on both bearing housings, classify the highest vibration result, and compare the temperature with the 70/80/90°C limits. Stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart if the highest vibration is classified in Zone D; an above-alarm bearing temperature again requires the site P1 response.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; stage one for paired bearing replacement if inspection or the section 5.3 high-temperature criterion requires replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; stage one so that both bearings can be replaced as a pair rather than changing only the drive-end bearing.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, require electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit after draining and venting.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For lifting the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, require a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment because the load exceeds 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain the specified Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry during any running checks or return-to-service activity.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the line is chemically dosed, require chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. Chemical dosing is not stated in the fault report.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If subsequent measurement places the highest housing vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Standard allowance for bearing replacement as a pair: 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, if paired replacement proceeds.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Standard allowance for laser alignment: 1.5 hours with 1 technician, required after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450, and manual Table 5 specifies 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead prohibits HF3-450 and requires cartridge seal HF3-450B at 30 Nm for HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-109 is HF3-23500, so it is inside that serial range and the bulletin governs any seal replacement on this asset. The bulletin also supplies the applicable sleeve criterion: replace HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth, whereas the manual only says to inspect for scoring. These seal requirements do not create a seal-replacement requirement for the present no-leakage report, but they must govern if seal work is added.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 2.5 mm/s an RMS vibration-velocity value measured on a bearing housing, and which housing was measured? Figure 3 applies only to mm/s RMS on bearing housings (C07).",
    "What is the vibration velocity on the other bearing housing? The manual requires classification of the highest reading from both housings, so the single reported value cannot complete that classification (C06).",
    "What are the actual grease quantity, bearing inspection findings and alignment measurements? These are needed to distinguish over-greasing, bearing wear and misalignment; the evidence does not rank their likelihood for this pump (C09).",
    "Is this a chemically dosed line? The report does not say, so the need for chemical goggles and nitrile gloves remains conditional (C15).",
    "Does the bearing-access method require opening the casing or disturbing the mechanical seal? The evidence gives the bearing pair-replacement rule but no bearing-replacement disassembly sequence, so any requirement for a casing gasket, seal parts or associated additional work must be confirmed before staging them (C05, C10).",
    "No standard labour times are supplied for diagnosis, isolation, lifting preparation or conditional seal/gasket work; only paired bearing replacement and laser alignment have documented allowances (C12).",
    "If the pump remains running pending repair, the required interim surveillance or operating restriction between the 80°C alarm and 90°C trip is not specified in the evidence and must be established rather than assumed (C02, C15)."
  ]
}
